In article 5zL@acsu.buffalo.edu, lerczak@acsu.buffalo.edu (Horse) writes:
>geas@castle.ed.ac.uk (S J Arnott) writes:
>
>>I am running nethack on sun4 (Displayed on sun3 (More of them)) while
>>running under openwindows 2 (Running tty graphics).
>>I can not seem to get the number pad to work properly.

Well that's simple, before you start the game you execute the 
commands: 

xmodmap -e "keysym R13 = 1"
xmodmap -e "keysym Down = 2"
xmodmap -e "keysym F35 = 3"
xmodmap -e "keysym Left = 4"
xmodmap -e "keysym F31 = 5"
xmodmap -e "keysym Right = 6"
xmodmap -e "keysym F27 = 7"
xmodmap -e "keysym Up = 8"
xmodmap -e "keysym F29 = 9"

And when you've finished you do:

xmodmap -e "keycode 119 = R13"
xmodmap -e "keycode 120 = Down"
xmodmap -e "keycode 121 = F35"
xmodmap -e "keycode  98 = Left"
xmodmap -e "keycode  99 = F31"
xmodmap -e "keycode 100 = Right"
xmodmap -e "keycode  75 = F27"
xmodmap -e "keycode  76 = Up"
xmodmap -e "keycode  77 = F29"

There is one drawback to this, if you use the number pad keys
in other programs before you have restored the keymap, they will
not work properly of course.

